   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "The composite has outer function F with \\( \\frac{d}{du} u^{3} = 3 u^{2} \\) and inner function \\( u = 6 - 2 x^{2} \\), whose derivative is \\( - 4 x \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99023",
         "rule_named": "identify the layers"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "By the product rule and the chain rule, \\( h'(x) = - 24 x^{3} \\left(6 - 2 x^{2}\\right)^{2} + 4 x \\left(6 - 2 x^{2}\\right)^{3} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99023",
         "rule_named": "product rule with the chain rule"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "At x = 1 the inner value is 4 and the inner derivative is -4, so \\( h'(1) = 256 + 2 \\cdot 48 \\cdot \\left(-4\\right) = -128 \\).",
